  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Pontoon Light",
    "description": "A stout black-and-yellow lighthouse on a low rock out in the water, reached only across a floating pontoon bridge: plank decks laid end to end over barrels. Its lantern and window light up after dark in World View. 21 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Rock** — two dark Brick 1x4s side by side make a low rock, 4 by 2, just out of the water, with Rocks round its foot.\n2. **Shore** — one stone Wide Stair on the shore steps up onto the bridge.\n3. **Pontoon Bridge** — two pairs of Barrels float in the water, and three wooden Plate 2x4s, turned 90° (press **R**), run end to end over them from the stair to the rock, meeting on the barrels.\n4. **Tower** — two Block 2x2s stacked black and yellow on the far half of the rock, so the bridge lands on open stone. The white Door, turned 90°, faces the bridge; a Small Window in the yellow band glows with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — a black Plate 2x2 for the gallery, a Lantern that lights up after dark, and a black Hip Roof.\n\nStand it with the stair on the shore and the rest out over the water: the pontoon is the only way across.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Rock: 2 Brick 1x4, 4 Rock\n- Shore: 1 Wide Stair\n- Pontoon Bridge: 4 Barrel, 3 Plate 2x4\n- Tower: 2 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Lantern: 1 Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Hip Roof\n\n21 bricks in all.\n",
